Grim reads the standard controller codes the Python port binds (PadCode in src/crimson/input_codes.py, 0x200 up) from
the joystick it polls, and names them (game/pad.cpp). The original Grim ignores these ids, so a crimson.cfg holding them
stays loadable by the 2003 executable.
